# chad-webui — invoke OpenWebUI REST API from inside the Chad sandbox.
#
# Wraps the v0.9+ OpenWebUI endpoints Chad uses to act on operator content:
# calendar, notes, automations, memories, chats, models, knowledge, folders.
# Output is JSON on stdout (parseable by the model); errors go to stderr with
# a non-zero exit code.
#
# Auth model
# ----------
# Two layers because OpenWebUI sits behind Cloudflare Access:
#   1. CF Access service token (header pair CF-Access-Client-{Id,Secret}) gets
#      past the edge. The CF Access policy must explicitly trust the service
#      token. Service tokens don't set Cf-Access-Authenticated-User-Email, so
#      OpenWebUI falls through to bearer-auth at layer 2.
#   2. OpenWebUI personal API key (Authorization: Bearer ...) authenticates
#      against an `auth.api_key` column row. The owning user's role determines
#      what the request can do. Use an admin key to give Chad ownership-bypass
#      on calendar/notes/etc.
#
# Credentials live in /sandbox/.nemoclaw/credentials.json:
#   {
#     "OPENWEBUI_API_KEY":        "<personal API key from /api/v1/auths/api_key>",
#     "CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID":      "<service token client id>.access",
#     "CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET":  "<service token secret>",
#     "OPENWEBUI_BASE_URL":       "https://chad.supachad.com/api/v1"   # optional
#   }
#
# Operator scoping
# ----------------
# When chad-shim launches `openclaw agent`, it exports CHAD_OPERATOR_SLUG (and
# CHAD_OPERATOR_EMAIL / CHAD_OPERATOR_ROLE / CHAD_OPERATOR_CHAT_ID for context).
# This wrapper reads CHAD_OPERATOR_SLUG and requires a matching key in
# credentials: OPENWEBUI_API_KEY_<SLUG.upper()>. If missing, the wrapper
# refuses to fall back to the default admin key — fail-closed enforcement.
# The result: OpenWebUI's own permission system contains a jailbroken or
# confused LLM, because cross-operator writes hit 403 at the API regardless
# of what the prompt says.
#
# Anonymous callers (no CHAD_OPERATOR_SLUG) get OPENWEBUI_API_KEY. Use a
# low-privilege key there if you want defense-in-depth for direct CLI use.

from __future__ import annotations

